{
  "thinking": "Empty table and nobody's proposed anything yet. A side-view fish facing right is easy for a judge to read, and a circle-based outline is simple to build. I'll claim the idea and start the back of the body from the tail end.",
  "say": "Right, I'd like to do a fish, side view, facing right. Round body, tail on the left. I'm starting the outline at the tail end and running it over the back toward the nose. Shout if you'd rather do something else, but I think a fish will read cleanly from across the room.",
  "to": "everyone",
  "eagerness": 8,
  "point": [25, 20],
  "do": "build",
  "strokes": [
    {"type": "arc", "cx": 32, "cy": 20, "r": 7, "a0": 180, "a1": 360, "spacing": 0.6}
  ],
  "start": true,
  "notes": "Plan: fish, side view, facing right, centred about (32,20), body radius 7. Build 1: top arc of body from tail end (25,20) over the back to nose (39,20), start domino here. Next: bottom arc (39,20) back to (25,20), then tail as two short lines from (25,20) out to about (17,13) and (17,27), joined at the body. Maybe an eye near (35,17) if there's time. Keep the chain continuous: check gaps before the push. Watch for others bumping the table near the body."
}

{
  "thinking": "The old start and the up-facing dominoes are cleared, so the top arc can go in. I'll build it from the tail at (25,20) over the back to the nose at (39,20) and tell the table what I'm doing.",
  "say": "Old start and the two up-facing dominoes are cleared. I'm building the top arc now, from the tail at (25,20) over the back to the nose at (39,20). Ava, I'll keep the tail end clear so your join lands on it.",
  "to": "everyone",
  "eagerness": 5,
  "point": [25, 20],
  "do": "build",
  "strokes": [
    {"type": "arc", "cx": 32, "cy": 20, "r": 7, "a0": 180, "a1": 360, "spacing": 0.55}
  ],
  "start": false,
  "notes": "Fish side view facing right, body centred (32,20), r=7. Top arc a0=180 to a1=360 from tail (25,20) over back to nose (39,20), about 37-40 dominoes; building now via build stroke. Old S at (24,19) and up-facing dominoes at (25,16)-(25,17) cleared. Chloe: tail and fins (lines to (17,13) and (17,27)). Ava: start at (8,20), spine to about (18,20), connects into my tail at (25,20). Start is Ava's (8,20); I'm not setting start:true. Dev: dorsal fin goes back on after body is up, around (24,18). Next: confirm top arc is standing, then bottom arc back to tail. Before the push: check the tail join and watch for bumps near the body."
}

{
  "thinking": "Ava's spine is nearly done at x=18, and Chloe is waiting to bridge. Dev still needs an answer: the up-facing dominoes at x=25, y=17 to 19 are my top arc, not leftovers. I'll say that, then carry the arc on from its end at (26,16).",
  "say": "Dev, those up-facing ones at x=25, y=17 to 19 are my top arc, rising from the tail at (25,20). They aren't the old start or the two I cleared. The old start and the originals are gone. I'm carrying the arc on from (26,16) and won't touch the body beyond it. Ava, got the spine. Chloe, bridge in when Ava calls x=18.",
  "to": "everyone",
  "eagerness": 7,
  "point": [25, 18],
  "do": "build",
  "strokes": [
    {"type": "extend", "from": [26, 16], "toward": [39, 20], "count": 30}
  ],
  "notes": "Start is Ava's (8,20); I'm not setting start:true. Old start (24,19) and the originals at (25,16)-(25,17) are cleared. Up-facing dominoes at (25,17)-(25,20) and (26,16) are my top arc, not leftovers; Dev has been told. Top arc: centre (32,20), r=7, tail (25,20) at 180, nose (39,20) at 360, about 40 dominoes. Extending from (26,16) toward (39,20), count 30, to finish it. Join from below, agreed with Dev and Chloe. Chloe's bridge comes from Ava's spine end at x=18 and must curve gently up into the tail. Knocker: domino at (25,20.7) facing up (270), added once the top arc is standing. Chloe: tail and fins, hands off the body until the join. Dev: dorsal fin around (24,18) once the body is standing; he'll inspect the corner. Ava: spine x=8 to 18, moves the start to her (8,20) last. Next: finish the top arc, add the (25,20.7) knocker, then build the bottom arc back to the tail. Before the push: check the tail join and watch for bumps near the body."
}

{
  "thinking": "Ava has cleared the bridge from x=18, and the map shows the tail at (25,20) standing and facing up. I'll connect from Ava's spine end into it so the join arrives from below, as agreed, and keep off Ben's arc above y=16.",
  "say": "Thanks, Ava, I'm clear from x=18. Ben, the tail at (25,20) is standing on the map, so I'm bridging into it from below so the fall turns up into your body. I'm keeping my hands off the arc above y=16.",
  "to": "everyone",
  "eagerness": 6,
  "point": [21, 21],
  "do": "build",
  "strokes": [
    {"type": "connect", "from": [18, 20], "to": [25, 20]}
  ],
  "start": false,
  "notes": "Fish, side view facing right. Start is to be set to Ava's (8,20) domino by Ava, last, after the join. Ava's spine: y=20, x=8 to 18, and she has cleared me to bridge from x=18. Ben's body: tail at (25,20), now standing up on the map. Arc rises from there over the back to nose (39,20); Ben is building from (26,16). Up-facing dominoes at x=25, y=16 to 19 are Ben's arc, not leftovers. Plan: I'm bridging with a connect from (18,20) to (25,20), arriving from below and turning up. Ben's knocker goes at about (25,20.7) facing up. Dev does the dorsal fin after the body is up and will inspect the corner. I'm keeping off the body and arc. Dominoes left: about 222."
}

{
  "thinking": "The map shows row 20 empty from x=19 to 24, and rows 21 to 23 are clear, so the strays Dev flagged are gone. Ben still has to re-stand (25,20.5), but connect routes behind whichever domino ends up nearest (25,20), so I can build the join now without waiting on the exact spacing.",
  "say": "Dev, Ben, Ava: the gap from (19,20) to (24,20) is clear, and rows 21 to 23 show nothing standing. I'm building a connect from Ava's (18,20) into Ben's tail at (25,20) now. Ben, keep off the knocker until I say the join's down, and tell us when (25,20.5) is re-stood. Ava, the start stays unset.",
  "to": "everyone",
  "eagerness": 6,
  "point": [21, 20],
  "do": "build",
  "strokes": [
    {"type": "connect", "from": [18, 20], "to": [25, 20]}
  ],
  "start": false,
  "notes": "13:15, 6.8 min left, 186 dominoes in the supply. Row 20 has a chain from x=8 to 18 (Ava's line, facing right, ends at 18). Gap is x=19 to 24 on row 20, now clear. Rows 21 to 23 look empty, so Dev's flagged strays appear gone. Ben's tail is at (25,20), with a re-stand of (25,20.5) pending. Building connect from (18,20) to (25,20). Don't touch x<=17, y<16, or the start. Knocker held by Ben, start unset at (8,20) held by Ava. Next: confirm the join, then check the tail spacing with Dev."
}
